  "name": "Trans_Body",
  "lookup_name": "Trans_Body",
  "title": "The Body",
  "description": "Three thresholds, and your own body is what opens each one. A corridor narrows to a wall of slats that stands shut and makes way exactly where you are standing, then closes again behind you. It narrows further to a solid block of small cubes that loses every cube you touch, so you melt a tunnel through it and the tunnel stays cut in the shape of the body that cut it. It narrows a third time to a field of blocks packed closer together than a pair of shoulders, which shrink as you come near and grow back once you are past. Nothing in this hall moves on its own. Every other room in the chapter shows you a cube being translated, turned or scaled while you watch; here the operator is you and the operand is the room, and the only way to find that out is to walk at it.",
